# Line-ending policy for this repo.
#
# This project has always been edited on Windows (CRLF), and that's the
# working-tree convention going forward. Left unconfigured, git guesses at
# line-ending handling per-checkout, which is what caused a whole-tree
# CRLF/LF mismatch between the working tree and a recent commit (every
# tracked file showed as "fully modified" even though `git diff -b` proved
# there were zero real content changes). This file pins the behavior so
# that doesn't happen again.
#
# Default: treat text files as text, normalize them internally for diffing,
# and check them out as CRLF (matching how this project is actually edited).
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Exception: shell scripts must stay LF. They run inside Linux containers
# (see r-backend/app/dev-start.sh) — a CRLF shebang/script line can break
# silently under `sh`/`bash` even though it looks fine in a Windows editor.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files — never treat as text, never diff, never convert.
*.rds binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
